WEBVTT

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.060
- No!
- ﻿You can't!

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:10.730
What is it?

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.360
Oh, Raraiya's a bit over energetic.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.110
Tell her to mind her manners.
We're guests on this ship.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:19.660
I'm terribly sorry.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.660
Mom, you haven't asked Inspector
General Gusion yet, have you?

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.670
W-We were in the middle of something.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.130
What's this about?

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:32.880
We want to enter the Capital
Territory with the Megafauna.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:33.920
Bellri!

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.050
What are you thinking?

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.090
If there really is a threat in space,

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:43.470
the Capital Army and Ameria
need to cooperate against it.

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.430
As amazing an idea as that is...

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:52.020
If the head of SU-Cordism would give us
information on the threat in space then—

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.990
I haven't heard anything about
that from His Holiness.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.110
However, to receive the Photon Batteries,

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:03.870
members of SU-Cordism periodically
go up to Sankt Porto.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.160
And as for the Rose of Hermes Blueprints—

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.170
- What is it?
- ﻿Nothing.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.840
Captain Donyell, using Minovsky
Flight to fly at low altitudes...

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.640
- That's possible, yeah?
- Huh?

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.050
Flying like that eats up the batteries.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:27.060
Once we reach land, I can
make a land line call.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.560
With that, I can call in a guide,
or rather, an escort for us.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.160
180 degree turn!

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.280
All hands, all baggage is secured, right?

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:54.710
Fixing course. Keeping her steady.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:04:00.130
Don't you think having no one to pilot the
Montero is putting a good suit to waste?

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.050
Huh? He's not here?

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.930
The Caribbean Ocean Laboratory
isn't a training academy!

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.530
Will Lieutenant Klim's
Armorzagan be all right?

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:23.200
Those two went prepared to act as decoys for us.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.870
- What is it?
- ﻿Mick's Armorzagan

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.910
seems to have shaken its pursuers.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.330
Good to hear.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.960
Is the Lieutenant returning home
due to pressure from the President?

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.500
No, it's for matters related
to the operation.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.260
- But that's wrong!
- No, it isn't!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.970
It's okay!

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.430
Entering the Izanellian Continent.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.350
All hands, we're getting close to
the Capital Territory!

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.600
Gisela.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:54.650
It's fine.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.770
I'm handling altitude
control over here as well.
You all understand that?

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.220
The director's headed out?

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.730
Did you say something?

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.440
I said it looks like this'll be fun.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.860
I haven't dressed like this in ages!

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.230
Bell! Mom!

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.530
This is just between us, but...

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.780
Yes?

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.240
I hear Bell was a foster child.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:52.200
What? You mean he was adopted?

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.710
I don't know the truth.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:57.460
That hurt!

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.090
Danger! Danger!

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.300
Don't scare me!

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.470
Come back over here!

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.640
- ﻿Is everything okay?
- ﻿Yeah.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.180
It's a long distance call, isn't it?

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.730
You realize the fees for
those are high, right?

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.270
Here, keep the change.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:19.440
Don't go over 20 minutes.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.070
Um, there's eleven in here, right?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.150
Could we have all of them?

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.530
- Huh?
- ﻿We'll give you a good price for them.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:30.990
The fish in the pen over there
are for sale too, right?

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.120
H-Hold on a moment.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.250
I'll go get the calculator.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.840
No! Don't eat Chuchumy!

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.760
- Kiran!
- ﻿She's got it wrong!

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:46.170
Kiran, you're a nurse.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:48.510
You should understand about Raraiya.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:52.260
My Bellri and Aida Surugan.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:00.040
Captain, please stabilize the ship!

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:05.280
Minovsky Flight is harder than
acting like pirates in space!

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.400
Are we really going to do a launch test here?

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:11.950
It's important that we're able
to launch no matter where we are.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.830
If we launch them unmanned, we can
still return them with autopilot.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.370
But if Minovsky Particles
are spread, that won't work.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.880
Why is there so much turbulence?

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.710
We're going at a low speed,
so the wind shakes us.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:30.090
Spaceships... are emblematic of...

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:36.560
They are emblematic of the technology
that led humanity to ruin.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:43.190
Do you think we can break through the
Capital Army's warning line on this course?

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.610
When I was on the phone earlier,

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:48.650
I called for the Capital
Guard to come pick us up.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.660
We can avoid the Army's eyes.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.540
He wants all hands to stay on alert
and prepared for combat.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:01.080
Isn't that weird? Since
we've got you people here.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.880
And the Operations Director of
Capital Tower is aboard as well.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:09.300
This is the southern continent,
Izanell. It's enemy territory.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.010
Quit talking about enemies
and enemy territory!

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.050
This is our homeland!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.640
I'm sorry, Miss Noredo Nug.

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:20.770
My... What a polite way to refer to me.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:21.850
How kind of you.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:23.900
Kind of you. Kind of you.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.730
Opening hangar doors.
Beware of strong winds.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.940
- ﻿Thank you.
- Any time.
Opening hangar doors.
Beware of strong winds.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:32.820
Okay, the Montero and Jahannam
are ready to launch.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.240
What are you saying, Happa?

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:37.240
I don't want to send out
that Jahannam unpiloted!

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:41.210
You mean Colonel Cumpa Rusita
of ﻿the Research Division?

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:44.460
Yes, he ought to be familiar
with the Rose of Hermes...

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.210
Hey, are those the Angel Falls?

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:51.220
No, there's lots of waterfalls
like that around these parts.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.220
They call this a waterfall?

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:02.850
What a laugh!

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:05.350
I heard that table mountains like this

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:08.780
are what let us hide from
Capital Tower's radar.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:10.440
Oh, sorry!

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.400
What are you apologizing for?

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:17.080
I started explaining something
any proper pilot should know.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.460
What?

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.880
She's fast. That's a proper pilot for you.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:37.850
That's no good! Steer!

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:39.850
If we accelerate, we'll trigger their radar!

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.060
Y-Yes, sir!

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.270
They've spread Minovsky Particles.

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.690
They're in the mood for a fight.

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:47.600
Steer, make a clean getaway for us!

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.650
Aye, aye, madam!

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.940
- Is it the Capital Army?
- ﻿I'm sorry.

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:53.860
Uh, no, it's fine.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.540
It transformed!

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.340
That's barely any damage! Again!

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:24.100
Where's Bell? I'm being useless!

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.310
I'm too slow!

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.270
That's the Mobile Suit from before.

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:32.570
No, is it a Mobile Armor?

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:39.450
To think I would chance upon you here.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:41.950
Now, I need despair no more, G-Self!

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:44.160
Miss Aida!

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:48.330
Accelerate!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:50.210
Don't send out the Jahannam.
It would be a waste!

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.420
- Do send out the Montero!
- ﻿Accelerating!

00:10:56.930 --> 00:11:00.550
We'll handle the Montero's friend
or foe identification by camera!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:03.060
It can use the Javelin at least, right?

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:04.600
Prepare to launch!

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.430
Let's get on with it. Go!

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:16.610
This guy again?!

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:26.660
An unmanned Mobile Suit?

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:28.290
G-Self!

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.550
That leaves you open!

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.900
Barara!

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.190
I won't let you get away!

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.440
Is this the end for me? Barara!

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:01.450
Reinforcements!

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.100
What?

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.100
A person?

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:45.280
If I can see a person, I can't shoot!

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:49.780
You shouldn't be doing that!

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:54.950
Barara!

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:56.910
Make it!

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.670
I can't see!

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:06.130
You've slid too far! Take us back!

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.340
There!

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.850
Brake a bit!

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:18.100
I said brake!

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.110
Barara!

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:26.900
We're withdrawing.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:28.360
Nicely done!

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:30.570
Take us straight back to Capital Tower!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.870
You'll need to bear with this for a while.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:34.910
Once things settle down,
I'll move to the cockpit.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.620
Oh... Okay!

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:40.000
First we should call
Colonel Cumpa for backup!

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.130
Pull away from the Megafauna!

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:55.430
Act as if we were directly
under Capital Tower.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:58.310
Mobile Suits are to stay
out there on combat alert.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.440
What about the Minovsky Particles?

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.690
They're starting to vanish, so I'm worried!

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:06.270
Fry-Schops stay prepped for combat as well!

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:11.530
G-Self, you suck! Don't
put dents in the deck!

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:14.410
Huh? Is Bell that bad at this?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.120
Maybe he's just tired from fighting?

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:20.710
Was it your planning that's
gotten us this far, Director?

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:22.370
Huh? Yeah...

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.670
The Capital Army and Guard
don't get along, you see.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.170
Oh.

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:31.680
Huh? What was that, Luan?

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:46.440
The Director is here, yes?

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.690
That voice...

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:50.360
Is that you, Instructor Kerbes Yoh?

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:53.070
Oh, Student Bellri Zenam.

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.950
That's our grade skipper!

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:56.950
You took back the G-Self!

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:59.200
...is not really something
I can say in this situation.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.870
Kerbes, thank you for your trouble.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:04.790
Did you recognize the F-Rug
that attacked this ship?

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.880
It's one of the Capital Army's.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:10.260
I saw it, but I don't
know the details myself.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:17.050
Student Bellri, have you become a
pilot for the Amerian Army now?

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.970
The Amerians won't give
me the rank of lieutenant,

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.270
so I'm still a Capital Guard cadet.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.310
If I recall...

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:26.980
You were the lady pirate, correct?

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.610
Yes.

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:30.690
Good of you to come.

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:35.410
Yeah, if I get a call straight from
the director, of course I'm coming out!

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.370
Along with some dummies to keep
this ship from being detected!

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.540
Huh?

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:52.130
We're almost at our destination.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.340
Follow the Single that's leading us.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:55.470
You can do that, right?

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:57.680
Huh? Who do you think you're talking to?

00:15:58.050 --> 00:15:59.510
Oh, sorry.

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:01.640
- Until later then, Director.
- ﻿Thank you.

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:05.810
Are the staff of the Capital
Guard all like that?

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:09.730
"The SU-Cordism faithful"
would be more correct.

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:12.650
Oh, SU-Cordism, huh?

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.420
Is it that small?

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:31.090
It's different from the impression
I got from the figures.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.460
Can you control it?

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:35.380
Take your measurements off.
Gisela, you too.

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:36.680
Fold in fins.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:38.220
Fin, put back!

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:40.220
Measuring distance.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:45.520
Hover jet landing!

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:47.230
- Okay.
- Five. Four.

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:03.200
Bridge pass.

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.330
Good. Next is the timing for the landing.

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.540
Okay. Hover brake!

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.330
Where have we landed?

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:12.420
Does it matter where?

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:23.640
Do it.

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:25.780
It flew!

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:40.490
Kerbes, I see you got to meet the director.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:42.320
She's right here!

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.490
Thank you for all your hard work.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:47.080
At the moment, we're carrying
the new photon batteries,

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.710
as well as water and air balls.

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:54.960
Father.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:57.210
Oh, it's Biclover.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:04.260
My house is nearby. Want to come stay there?

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:05.970
House? Stay?

00:18:05.970 --> 00:18:08.140
- You can stay.
- ﻿What are those trailers for?

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:15.150
Those trailers carry photon batteries
to the airport to be shipped worldwide.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.820
Once the batteries are
loaded on the trailers,

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.650
my mother's work is done.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.570
We should have just kept going.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:27.870
F-Rugs must not go near Biclover.

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.710
Well, the Capital Army are
doing it, aren't they?

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:31.290
The Army are like a bunch of gangsters.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.040
F-Rugs can't dance! Get that thing out of here!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.130
I have not permitted it.

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:39.010
- Can you handle it?
- ﻿I'll be fine.

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.260
Okay, you can go!

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:42.840
We'll be heading off too.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:50.060
Get off that Shank and dance!

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.770
- Let's dance!
- ﻿Come on!

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:54.730
Come on! Come on!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.610
There's more to life than work!

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.730
This looks to me like a
society ruined by abundance.

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:01.860
Work at Capital Tower is hard.

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:04.740
They need a chance to let
it all out once a week.

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:25.090
This is your ID Card, Miss Aida Surugan.

00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:26.300
Thank you.

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:27.890
Mr. Gusion Surugan.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:29.180
Thank you.

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:32.730
You mean to tell me you weren't
monitoring because it's the weekend?

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.350
Is that a joke?

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:37.690
Colonel! Can I call my boyfriend over?

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:39.980
I've already told you
to do whatever you want!

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:41.740
Tell Mask to take a rest.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:43.030
Yes.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:45.780
I want to arrange a meeting between
Mask and Commander Jugan.

00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:49.780
What? Not until the weekend is over?

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:52.620
Some Capital Army!

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:57.210
These Earthnoids belong on the list
of organisms that ought to go extinct.

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:03.590
Have you just returned
from your business trip?

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:07.800
Yes. Your Holiness, I would like
you to explain everything you know

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:11.470
in regards to the coming threat from space.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.020
Why, it's Miss Noredo Nug.

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:17.350
- Oh, hello!
- ﻿You seem well.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.060
Yes, Your Holiness.

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:22.860
Wonderful. I pray that it
will ever remain so.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:27.570
Capital Tower will not
be destroyed by anyone.

00:20:27.570 --> 00:20:32.740
What my father wants to ask is if
there are forces coming from space.

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:37.920
Throughout the Reguild Century,
it has been the mercy of SU-Cordism,

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:41.000
that has allowed the Capital Tower to operate.

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.880
However, in the teachings of SU-Cordism,

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:49.430
it is never said that Capital
Tower links us to people in space.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:51.600
For you to face each new day on Earth,

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:54.810
must we start by explaining
the elements in the air?

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:59.560
Did you imagine photon batteries naturally
sprang into existence up in space?

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:01.440
The photon batteries

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:04.690
are not something we Earthnoids
can disassemble or repair.

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:07.110
If we try, they explode.

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:09.570
That's why doing so was made taboo.

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:12.580
That creates the evil of monopolization.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:16.370
We of Ameria wish to liberate the world
from Capital Tower's monopoly and—

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:18.830
That kind of thinking is the true threat.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.290
- ﻿That's—
- ﻿Wilmit Zenam.

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:23.800
I wasn't aware you had returned.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.920
Colonel Cumpa! Were you not
supposed to be off for the weekend?

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:29.930
And what is Inspector General
Surugan doing here as well?

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:32.510
I have a question, Colonel Cumpa.

00:21:32.510 --> 00:21:35.560
The Rose of Hermes Blueprints...

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.230
You were aware of their existence, yes.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:39.730
That's a rather fantastical name.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:42.810
I beg your pardon for the interruption.

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:45.110
<i>﻿He's the top of the Research Division,</i>

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:47.110
<i>﻿and the man pulling the strings
behind the Capital Army...</i>

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:48.320
Cadet Bellri Zenam!

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:50.320
There you are!

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:52.780
What is it?

00:21:53.530 --> 00:21:54.780
Miss Aida as well!

00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:58.620
Yes. Ma'am, take care of my father.

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:00.040
Aida Surugan!

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:02.540
You'll trip!

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:04.960
What? What did you say?

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:03.200
With the Capital Army after us,

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:07.790
hard work on Aida's part wouldn't be
enough to let the Megafauna escape.

00:24:07.790 --> 00:24:09.460
The reason we were able to do it,

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:13.130
isn't because of the capabilities
of the G-Self's High Torque Pack,

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:15.380
but because of my idea.

00:24:17.050 --> 00:24:19.590
On the next episode of Reconguista in G,

00:24:19.600 --> 00:24:20.970
Escape from the Territory.

00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:24.520
Watch and I'll show you what a genius I am!
